;; spec:   stdlib §5.5 S5, §2.7, §7 L24 (joins and families)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 1
;; audit:  clean
;; open:   L24
;; Clojure's (= [1] (list 1)) is true: two sequential collections are equal
;; when their elements are. `=` has one type today: `cannot unify (Vec
;; i64) with (List i64)`; L24 elaborates it to a sequence comparison when
;; both operands are of one family (A11 n4). The first refusal today is
;; older: `no implementation of Eq for (Vec i64)`, which L3 lifts; this case
;; stays open until the family rule too has landed.
(defun main () -> i64
  (if (= [1] (list 1)) 1 0))
